# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Database
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local development runs Postgres in Docker, NOT a branch of a Neon project
# (ADR-0075 §1, #906). `bun run db:up` starts it; see docker-compose.yml, which
# also explains the port — 5433, not 5432.
#
# Fill these in like every other value in this file. This is the one that has no
# console behind it: the user, password and database name are the POSTGRES_USER,
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD and POSTGRES_DB of docker-compose.yml, and the port is the
# one it publishes. A connection string is a secret (CLAUDE.md → Hard Rules),
# so no working one is committed here — not even this one.
#
# Locally the two URLs are the same plain Postgres string — there is no pooler
# in front of the container. In the deployed (Neon) environments they differ,
# and the difference matters:
#   DATABASE_URL — POOLED (-pooler host, pgbouncer=true). Used at runtime by
#                  PrismaService for queries.
#   DIRECT_URL   — DIRECT (no -pooler, no pgbouncer). Used by the Prisma CLI /
#                  schema `directUrl` for migrations (migrate deploy needs a
#                  session-level connection that pgbouncer's transaction
#                  pooling breaks).
# Neon strings also carry connect_timeout=15 & pool_timeout=15, because Neon
# scales the compute to zero when idle and a cold resume (~5–10s) exceeds
# Prisma's 5s default and times out (#612). Docker has no cold start, so
# local needs no timeout tuning.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://<user>:<password>@localhost:5433/<database>"
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://<user>:<password>@localhost:5433/<database>"

# Clerk secret key — find in Clerk dashboard → API Keys
CLERK_SECRET_KEY="sk_test_..."

# Cloudflare R2 — find in R2 dashboard → Manage R2 API tokens.
# Local dev uses its OWN dedicated dev buckets + a dev-scoped token — NEVER the
# prod token. Each environment has its own public + documents bucket pair:
#   local:   gigloop-dev-public      / gigloop-dev-documents      (dev token)
#   preprod: gigloop-preprod-public  / gigloop-preprod-documents  (preprod token)
#   prod:    gigloop-public          / gigloop-documents          (prod token)
R2_ACCOUNT_ID="..."
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID="..."
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY="..."
# Public assets bucket (musician logos/photos) — public access ENABLED.
# The `-public` suffix is a safety signal: anything here is world-readable,
# so NEVER store sensitive data (contracts, invoices, PII) in it. Those go in
# the private R2_DOCUMENTS_BUCKET_NAME bucket below (ADR-0059).
R2_BUCKET_NAME="gigloop-dev-public"
# Public URL for the assets bucket (custom domain or the r2.dev subdomain).
# Must match R2_BUCKET_NAME — logoUrl/photo are stored as full URLs, so this
# host is baked into saved rows and sent-email <img> tags.
R2_PUBLIC_URL="https://pub-xxx.r2.dev"
# Private bucket for Documents (contracts, invoices, uploads, song lists) —
# public access DISABLED. Served only via access-controlled, presigned GETs
# (ADR-0059). No public URL: objects are never world-readable. Uses the same
# R2_ACCOUNT_ID / access keys above (the token must be scoped to this bucket
# too). Assets (logos/photos) stay in R2_BUCKET_NAME.
R2_DOCUMENTS_BUCKET_NAME="gigloop-dev-documents"

# AES-256-GCM key for encrypting bankDetails at rest.
# Must be exactly 64 hex characters (32 bytes).
# Generate with: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
ENCRYPTION_KEY="<64-hex-chars>"

# Resend — find API key in Resend dashboard → API Keys
# RESEND_FROM is a bare address only (never "Name <email>") — client-facing sends prepend
# the musician's own name in code (#932), so a wrapped value here would double up.
# For development use onboarding@resend.dev (only delivers to your Resend account email)
# For production use a verified domain address, e.g. bookings@gigloop.app — not noreply@,
# since these are genuinely two-way now (Reply-To routes replies to the musician)
RESEND_API_KEY="re_..."
RESEND_FROM="onboarding@resend.dev"

# Redirect ALL outbound mail to this address (dev/preprod safety). Default-off:
# unset → send to the real recipient (prod). Set in preprod so the synthetic-data
# smoke-test env can never email a real customer. Applies to both single and batch sends.
MAIL_REDIRECT_TO=

# Base URL of the frontend app — used to construct portal links in emails
# e.g. http://localhost:5173 for development, https://app.gigman.com for production
APP_BASE_URL="http://localhost:5173"

# Allowed CORS origin for the API — set to the frontend URL in production
# e.g. https://app.gigman.com; falls back to http://localhost:5173 in development
CORS_ORIGIN="https://app.gigman.com"

# Google Maps Distance Matrix API key — required for travel time calculation
# Obtain at: https://console.cloud.google.com → APIs & Services → Credentials
# Enable "Distance Matrix API" for the key
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY="AIza..."

# Example feature flag (see src/common/featureFlags.ts for the convention).
# Default-off: unset, empty, "false", or "0" all resolve to off; "true" or
# "1" turns it on.
FEATURE_EXAMPLE=

# E2E test mode (ADR-0048 / src/common/test-mode.ts). When "true"/"1" the API
# boots with fake outbound adapters (R2 → in-memory, Resend → sink, Google Maps
# → fixed distance) so the Playwright suite drives the real frontend + real API
# + ephemeral DB without touching third parties. The real Clerk AuthGuard is
# NEVER faked. Set only by the e2e harness — leave OFF everywhere else (prod,
# preprod, local dev).
E2E_TEST_MODE=

# Synthetic user id for `bun run seed` (prisma/seed.ts). Must equal a real
# Clerk-dev user id in the environment the seed is run against, or the
# AuthGuard scopes queries to the signed-in user and the seeded data is
# invisible after sign-in (ADR-0044 §7). Defaults to Tim's own Clerk dev
# user id for local seeding when unset.
SEED_USER_ID=

# Sentry error alerting (ADR-0077). Find the DSN in Sentry → Project Settings
# → Client Keys. Gated purely by presence — unset locally (off), set in both
# preprod and prod so 5xx exceptions from AllExceptionsFilter are captured.
SENTRY_DSN=

# Explicit environment tag for Sentry events — "preprod" or "prod". NOT derived
# from Railway's auto-injected RAILWAY_ENVIRONMENT_NAME: Railway's prod
# environment is still literally named "production" (#947), so reading that
# var would silently mistag prod events and the prod-only alert rule would
# never fire. Set by hand in Railway alongside SENTRY_DSN.
SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT=
